!AGENTS.md
.pi/

# openspec/ is gitignored globally (in ~/.config/git/ignore) so foreign
# projects don't accidentally commit scratch artifacts. In sysinit itself
# we own the schema fork and historical changes, so they should be tracked.
!openspec/

# Same reasoning for ast-grep. `**/sgconfig.yml` and `ast-grep/` are gitignored
# globally so a scratch rule set in a foreign project is never committed. Here
# they are the rule library this repository ships to ~/.config/ast-grep/ and the
# project root that `nix flake check` gates, so both have to be tracked. An
# untracked file is absent from the flake source and the check fails on it.
!sgconfig.yml
!modules/home/programs/ast-grep/

